# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# Benjamin twos (Wikipedia, "Benjamin Twos"; the PBS scenario
# `Benjamin_2D`): 2♣ is a strong two that is not forcing to game, 2♦ is
# the game-forcing opening, and there is no weak 2♦ (preempts.bid,
# `weak_2d_open`). The 2♣ openings of strong-openings.bid are off.
#
#   2♣  22-23, or an unbalanced 20+ with a good six-card suit or a
#       strong two-suiter and at most four losers
#   2♦  24+, or 23 without a five-card suit, or 22+ with one loser
#
# The ranges are BBA's (Benjamin_2D: 2♣ 20-23 and every distributional
# powerhouse, 2♦ 24+ and some 23s without a long suit); Wikipedia and
# the PBS chat put game-in-hand hands in 2♦.
#
# Responses to 2♣ are those of strong-openings.bid (2♦ waiting, the
# positives, the second negative). Responses to 2♦ (PBS): 2NT negative
# (0-6), 2♥/2♠ five or more, 3♣/3♦ six or more, any strength, 3NT 7+
# without a long suit. See benjamin.notes.md.

module benjamin "Benjamin 2♣ and 2♦"
  card   two_level.benjamin.play
  needs  strong-openings
  skill  bidding_conventions/benjamin_2d

when opening
  2C  "Benjamin 2♣: 22-23, or a strong two (about nine tricks)"   alert
      shows hcp=22..23 | (!balanced, hcp=20..23, losers<=4, (S>=6, quality(S)>=good) | (H>=6, quality(H)>=good) | (D>=6, quality(D)>=good) | (C>=6, quality(C)>=good) | shape 5-5-x-x | shape 6-5-x-x)
      sets  forcing=game, ask=strong_2c
      artificial
      priority 1
  2D  "Benjamin 2♦: game forcing, 24+"   alert
      shows hcp>=24 | (hcp=23, longest<=4)
      sets  forcing=game, ask=benjamin
      artificial
      priority 1
  # Game in hand (Wikipedia: 2♦ is the game force on playing tricks):
  # BBA opens 2♦ with 22-23 and at most one loser (Benjamin_2D: 4 of 4).
  2D  "Benjamin 2♦: game in hand, 22+ and at most one loser"   alert
      shows hcp>=22, losers<=1
      sets  forcing=game, ask=benjamin
      artificial
      priority 2

# ── Responder to 2♣ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Benjamin's 2♣ is forcing for one round, and passable after opener's
# rebid. We keep the strong 2♣'s game force and its second negative
# (strong-openings.bid) for now: written as passable, half of the
# continuations had no rule (benjamin.notes.md). A raise of opener's
# major after the waiting 2♦ agrees it.
after 2C (P) 2D (P) 2M (P)
  3M  "Three or more {M}: a raise with some values"   shows M>=3, hcp>=4
      sets  trump=M
      priority 1

# ── Responder to 2♦ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PBS chat (Benjamin_2D.btn): 2NT is the negative, "5- HCP, no 5-card
# major"; 2♥/2♠ five or more, 3♣/3♦ six or more, with no strength
# floor (the 5+ HCP is the chat's 2♣ responses; until 2026-10-07 we read
# it into 2♦ too and bid 2NT with a weak five-card major, notes). BBA
# (Benjamin_2D corpus): every five-card major bids it, 0-13 HCP; a
# six-card minor bids it from 1 HCP; without either 2NT up to 6 and 3NT
# from 7.
when asked benjamin
  2S  "Five or more spades (any strength)"         shows S>=5, S>=H
  2H  "Five or more hearts (any strength)"         shows H>=5, H>S
  3C  "Six or more clubs, no five-card major"      shows C>=6, C>=D, H<=4, S<=4
  3D  "Six or more diamonds, no five-card major"   shows D>=6, D>C, H<=4, S<=4
  3N  "Positive: 7+ HCP, no five-card major or six-card minor"   shows hcp>=7, H<=4, S<=4, D<=5, C<=5
  2N  "Negative: 0-6, no five-card major or six-card minor"      artificial
      priority -1

# ── Opener after a positive suit ─────────────────────────────────────
# Game is forced; opener has 24+, so the questions are the fit and the
# strain (BBA raises with three, else shows a suit or bids notrump). The
# raise agrees the suit, and the slam modules take over (keycards).
# Until 2026-10-07 opener had no rule here and the base 3NT ended the
# auction (Benjamin_2D: 2♦-2♥-3NT-pass on boards with a grand slam).
after 2D (P) 2y (P) | 2D (P) 3y (P) when y is not N
  cheapest(y) "Raise: three or more {y}"   shows y>=3   sets trump=y
      priority 1
  cheapest(S) "Five or more spades"        shows S>=5   when y is not S
  cheapest(H) "Five or more hearts"        shows H>=5   when y is not H
  cheapest(D) "Five or more diamonds"      shows D>=5   when y is not D
  cheapest(C) "Five or more clubs"         shows C>=5   when y is not C
  cheapest(N) "No fit, no suit to show"
      priority -1

# Responder after opener's raise of the major: with 0-5 the fast arrival
# to game (BBA: 4 of 4 with 0-6 there, two of them 3NT); more cue-bids
# (control-bids.bid) or asks.
after 2D (P) 2M (P) 3M (P)
  4M  "Weak: 0-5, game"    shows hcp<=5
      priority 2

# Opener over responder's game in the agreed major (0-5 after the raise,
# 0-6 after the negative): slam needs the playing tricks, at most two
# losers (BBA: asked on 4 of 4 with two or fewer, passed 5 of 6 with
# three or more, Benjamin_2D). With fewer the generic keycard ask
# (rkcb-1430.bid, 18 of my own) asks anyway.
after 2D (P) 2M (P) 3M (P) 4M (P) | 2D (P) 2N (P) 3M (P) 4M (P)
  P   "Game: partner is weak and I have three losers or more"   shows losers>=3
      priority 1

# Responder after opener's suit: raise with three (agreeing it), rebid a
# six-card major or a seven-card minor, else notrump. (A six-card minor
# rebid at the four level left opener without a rule: four boards.)
after 2D (P) 2y (P) 2z (P) | 2D (P) 2y (P) 3z (P) | 2D (P) 3y (P) 3z (P) when y is not N, z is not N, z is not y
  cheapest(z) "Three or more {z}: agrees it"   shows z>=3   sets trump=z
      priority 1
  cheapest(y) "Six or more {y}"                shows y>=6
      when  y is H | y is S
  cheapest(y) "Seven or more {y}"              shows y>=7
      when  y is C | y is D
  cheapest(N) "No fit"
      priority -1

# ── Opener over the 3NT positive ─────────────────────────────────────
# 24+ facing 7+: slam is there. BBA (Benjamin_2D, 41 boards) bids slam
# on every one: mostly 5NT, which responder answers 6NT, or 7NT with a
# maximum; 6NT or 7NT directly with more.
after 2D (P) 3N (P)
  7N  "Grand slam: 37 or more between us"   shows hcp + partner.hcp.min >= 37
      priority 3
  5N  "Slam: 6NT, or 7NT with a maximum"    shows hcp>=23
      sets  forcing=game
      priority 2
after 2D (P) 3N (P) 5N (P)
  7N  "A maximum: 12+ HCP"    shows hcp>=12
      priority 1
  6N  "6NT"

# ── Opener after the negative 2NT: natural ───────────────────────────
after 2D (P) 2N (P)
  3C  "Five or more clubs"       shows C>=5
  3D  "Five or more diamonds"    shows D>=5
  3H  "Five or more hearts"      shows H>=5
  3S  "Five or more spades"      shows S>=5
  3N  "Balanced"                 shows balanced
      priority 1
  4N  "Balanced 28+: invites 6NT"   shows balanced, hcp>=28
      sets  ask=quant
      priority 2

# Responder after opener's suit over the negative: raise with three
# (agreeing it: opener's 24+ then asks for keycards), else 3NT.
after 2D (P) 2N (P) 3z (P) when z is not N
  4z  "Three or more {z}"    shows z>=3   sets trump=z
      when  z is H | z is S
      priority 1
  3N  "No fit"
